</figure>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Algorithm <a href="#alg3" title="Algorithm 3 ‣ Appendix B Full Sampling Algorithm ‣ Self-Speculative Masked Diffusions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> consists of an outer loop each corresponding to one forward pass of the non-causal layers and an inner speculative sampling loop with <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> iterations. When the current number of revealed tokens is <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, the outer loop starts with a forward pass of the non-causal blocks to obtain the draft distribution for the currently masked tokens up to a maximum length specified by the window function, <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\overset{\leftrightarrow}{p}_{\theta}(\hat{\bm{x}}^{\sigma(i+1:\text{min}(i+W(i),D))}|\theta(\bm{x}^{\sigma(1:i)}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">↔</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mtext>min</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overset{\leftrightarrow}{p}_{\theta}(\hat{\bm{x}}^{\sigma(i+1:\text{min}(i+W(i),D))}|\theta(\bm{x}^{\sigma(1:i)}))</annotation></semantics></math>. The algorithm then begins the <math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> inner speculative sampling loops.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The inner speculative sampling loop begins with a forward pass of the causal layers re-using the non-causal hidden states that were computed on <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{x}^{\sigma(1:i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}^{\sigma(1:i)}</annotation></semantics></math>. In addition, the causal layers get access to the values of the drafted tokens. The causal probabilities are then of the form</p>
<table id="A2.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{\overset{\rightarrow}{p}_{\theta,\phi}(\hat{\bm{x}}^{\sigma(d)}|\theta(\bm{x}^{\sigma(1:i)}),\phi(\hat{\bm{x}}^{\sigma(i+1:d-1)}))\}_{d=j+1}^{\text{min}(i+W(i),D)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mtext>min</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\overset{\rightarrow}{p}_{\theta,\phi}(\hat{\bm{x}}^{\sigma(d)}|\theta(\bm{x}^{\sigma(1:i)}),\phi(\hat{\bm{x}}^{\sigma(i+1:d-1)}))\}_{d=j+1}^{\text{min}(i+W(i),D)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">With these target probabilities, a speculative sampling procedure can then be run which will accept some number of the draft tokens. Once a rejection occurs, that draft token is resampled from the resample probability distribution</p>
<table id="A2.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{p}(\hat{\bm{x}}^{\sigma(d)})\propto\text{max}\left(0,\overset{\rightarrow}{p}_{\theta,\phi}(\hat{\bm{x}}^{\sigma(d)}|\theta(\bm{x}^{\sigma(1:i)}),\phi(\hat{\bm{x}}^{\sigma(i+1:d-1)}))-\overset{\leftrightarrow}{p}_{\theta}(\hat{\bm{x}}^{\sigma(d)}|\theta(\bm{x}^{\sigma(1:i)}))\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mtext>max</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">↔</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{p}(\hat{\bm{x}}^{\sigma(d)})\propto\text{max}\left(0,\overset{\rightarrow}{p}_{\theta,\phi}(\hat{\bm{x}}^{\sigma(d)}|\theta(\bm{x}^{\sigma(1:i)}),\phi(\hat{\bm{x}}^{\sigma(i+1:d-1)}))-\overset{\leftrightarrow}{p}_{\theta}(\hat{\bm{x}}^{\sigma(d)}|\theta(\bm{x}^{\sigma(1:i)}))\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">The token <math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\bm{x}}^{\sigma(d)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\bm{x}}^{\sigma(d)}</annotation></semantics></math> is set to this new value that has been sampled from <math id="A2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{p}(\hat{\bm{x}}^{\sigma(d)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{p}(\hat{\bm{x}}^{\sigma(d)})</annotation></semantics></math>. The next iteration of speculative sampling can then begin. We perform another forward pass of the causal layers using the same non-causal hidden states as before. However, due to the resampling, one of the draft tokens has changed value and hence the causal probabilities are different than the previous speculative sampling loop. We repeat the speculative sampling procedure with these new causal target probabilities, noting the non-causal draft probabilities remain unchanged however.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">These speculative sampling loops repeat until either <math id="A2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> loops have been completed or <math id="A2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{min}(i+W(i),D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>min</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{min}(i+W(i),D)</annotation></semantics></math> tokens have been revealed. In the next outer iteration, the non-causal layers are applied to the currently revealed tokens including those that were just revealed in the prior <math id="A2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> speculative sampling inner loops and the algorithm repeats.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Proofs</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition 3.1. ‣ 3.4 Theoretical Results ‣ 3 Self-Speculative Masked Diffusions ‣ Self-Speculative Masked Diffusions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We aim to find the likelihood assigned to a given datapoint <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{x}^{1:D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}^{1:D}</annotation></semantics></math> under the generative model defined by models <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overset{\rightarrow}{p}_{\theta,\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overset{\rightarrow}{p}_{\theta,\phi}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overset{\leftrightarrow}{p}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">↔</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overset{\leftrightarrow}{p}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, sampling Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ 3.3 Sampling Procedure ‣ 3 Self-Speculative Masked Diffusions ‣ Self-Speculative Masked Diffusions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and ordering <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>. Let us first start by assuming that we have a fixed linear ordering <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=\{1,\dots,D\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=\{1,\dots,D\}</annotation></semantics></math> for simplicity. We let <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the event that for the <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-th dimension, we accepted the draft token in the speculative sampling procedure. Let <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> correspondingly denote the event that in the <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-th dimension we rejected the draft token.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We note that if we have event <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, then for dimension <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d+1</annotation></semantics></math> we will be continuing in the same speculative sampling loop as for dimension <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>. If we have event <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, on the other hand, we will exit the speculative sampling loop at dimension <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> and then enter into the next iteration of the outer loop in Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ 3.3 Sampling Procedure ‣ 3 Self-Speculative Masked Diffusions ‣ Self-Speculative Masked Diffusions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. The significance of this outer loop iteration change is that the draft distribution changes from <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\overset{\leftrightarrow}{p}_{\theta}(\bm{x}^{i+1:D}|\theta(\bm{x}^{1:i}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">↔</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overset{\leftrightarrow}{p}_{\theta}(\bm{x}^{i+1:D}|\theta(\bm{x}^{1:i}))</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\overset{\leftrightarrow}{p}_{\theta}(\bm{x}^{d+1:D}|\theta(\bm{x}^{1:d}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">↔</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overset{\leftrightarrow}{p}_{\theta}(\bm{x}^{d+1:D}|\theta(\bm{x}^{1:d}))</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d&gt;i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d&gt;i</annotation></semantics></math> meaning additional context is now revealed to the non-causal blocks. In other words, once we have a rejection, then the draft distribution will update with all the new tokens that were produced in the previous speculative sampling run. Therefore, in order to know the correct distribution that is being used as the draft, we need to know when our last rejection was to know what conditioning information is being input into the non-causal blocks.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In order to make headway into this problem, we utilize a recursive decomposition approach exploiting the fact that the likelihood of <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of all accept/reject decisions prior to the most recent reject decision. This is because <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overset{\leftrightarrow}{p}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">↔</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overset{\leftrightarrow}{p}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overset{\rightarrow}{p}_{\theta,\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overset{\rightarrow}{p}_{\theta,\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> depend only on the currently revealed tokens <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{x}^{1:i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}^{1:i}</annotation></semantics></math> and not the exact path taken to generate those tokens.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">In our proof, we will let <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Y</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be the result of the accept/reject step for dimension <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> i.e. <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y^{d}\in\{A^{d},R^{d}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y^{d}\in\{A^{d},R^{d}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. As a shorthand, we will sometimes simply write <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> to mean <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y^{d}=A^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y^{d}=A^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> to mean <math id="A3.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y^{d}=R^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y^{d}=R^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We start by introducing some marginalization over the accept/reject decisions,</p>
<table id="A3.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\theta,\phi}(\bm{x}^{1:D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\theta,\phi}(\bm{x}^{1:D})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E16.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{Y^{1:D}}p_{\theta,\phi}(\bm{x}^{1:D},Y^{1:D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{Y^{1:D}}p_{\theta,\phi}(\bm{x}^{1:D},Y^{1:D})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E17.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{Y^{1:D-1}}p_{\theta,\phi}(\bm{x}^{1:D},Y^{1:D-1},A^{D})+\sum_{Y^{1:D-1}}p_{\theta,\phi}(\bm{x}^{1:D},Y^{1:D-1},R^{D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{Y^{1:D-1}}p_{\theta,\phi}(\bm{x}^{1:D},Y^{1:D-1},A^{D})+\sum_{Y^{1:D-1}}p_{\theta,\phi}(\bm{x}^{1:D},Y^{1:D-1},R^{D})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E18.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{Y^{1:D-1}}p_{\theta,\phi}(\bm{x}^{1:D},Y^{1:D-1},A^{D})+p_{\theta,\phi}(\bm{x}^{1:D},R^{D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{Y^{1:D-1}}p_{\theta,\phi}(\bm{x}^{1:D},Y^{1:D-1},A^{D})+p_{\theta,\phi}(\bm{x}^{1:D},R^{D})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E19.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{Y^{1:D-2}}p_{\theta,\phi}(\bm{x}^{1:D},Y^{1:D-2},A^{D-1},A^{D})+\sum_{Y^{1:D-2}}p_{\theta,\phi}(\bm{x}^{1:D},Y^{1:D-2},R^{D-1},A^{D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{Y^{1:D-2}}p_{\theta,\phi}(\bm{x}^{1:D},Y^{1:D-2},A^{D-1},A^{D})+\sum_{Y^{1:D-2}}p_{\theta,\phi}(\bm{x}^{1:D},Y^{1:D-2},R^{D-1},A^{D})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+p_{\theta,\phi}(\bm{x}^{1:D},R^{D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+p_{\theta,\phi}(\bm{x}^{1:D},R^{D})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E21.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{Y^{1:D-2}}p_{\theta,\phi}(\bm{x}^{1:D},Y^{1:D-2},A^{D-1},A^{D})+p_{\theta,\phi}(\bm{x}^{1:D},R^{D-1},A^{D})+p_{\theta,\phi}(\bm{x}^{1:D},R^{D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{Y^{1:D-2}}p_{\theta,\phi}(\bm{x}^{1:D},Y^{1:D-2},A^{D-1},A^{D})+p_{\theta,\phi}(\bm{x}^{1:D},R^{D-1},A^{D})+p_{\theta,\phi}(\bm{x}^{1:D},R^{D})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\vdots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">⋮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\vdots</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E23.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\theta,\phi}(\bm{x}^{1:D},A^{1:D})+\sum_{d=1}^{D}p_{\theta,\phi}(\bm{x}^{1:D},R^{d},A^{d+1:D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\theta,\phi}(\bm{x}^{1:D},A^{1:D})+\sum_{d=1}^{D}p_{\theta,\phi}(\bm{x}^{1:D},R^{d},A^{d+1:D})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E24.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\theta,\phi}(\bm{x}^{1:D},A^{1:D})+\sum_{d=1}^{D}p_{\theta,\phi}(\bm{x}^{1:d},R^{d})p_{\theta,\phi}(\bm{x}^{d+1:D},A^{d+1:D}|\bm{x}^{1:d},R^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\theta,\phi}(\bm{x}^{1:D},A^{1:D})+\sum_{d=1}^{D}p_{\theta,\phi}(\bm{x}^{1:d},R^{d})p_{\theta,\phi}(\bm{x}^{d+1:D},A^{d+1:D}|\bm{x}^{1:d},R^{d})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p">The distribution <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\theta,\phi}(\bm{x}^{d+1},A^{d+1:D}|\bm{x}^{1:d},R^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta,\phi}(\bm{x}^{d+1},A^{d+1:D}|\bm{x}^{1:d},R^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> is easy to calculate because it is the probability of generating the given <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{x}^{d+1:D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}^{d+1:D}</annotation></semantics></math> and all of them being accepted when the last rejection was <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the last rejection is the same for all the <math id="A3.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d+1:D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d+1:D</annotation></semantics></math> dimensions, the conditioning information for the draft model is not changing since all the dimensions are being generated in the same inner speculative sampling procedure.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Specifically, we have</p>
<table id="A3.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\theta,\phi}(\bm{x}^{d+1:D},A^{d+1:D}|\bm{x}^{1:d},R^{d})=\prod_{k=d+1}^{D}p_{\theta,\phi}(A^{k},\bm{x}^{k}|x^{1:k-1},R^{d},A^{d+1:k-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>D</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\theta,\phi}(\bm{x}^{d+1:D},A^{d+1:D}|\bm{x}^{1:d},R^{d})=\prod_{k=d+1}^{D}p_{\theta,\phi}(A^{k},\bm{x}^{k}|x^{1:k-1},R^{d},A^{d+1:k-1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p">We now introduce Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma C.1. ‣ C.1 Proof of Proposition ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Self-Speculative Masked Diffusions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a> that allows us to compute the joint probability of having an acceptance in position <math id="A3.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> and the output token having value <math id="A3.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.1</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For a single speculative sampling accept/reject step with target distribution <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overset{\rightarrow}{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overset{\rightarrow}{p}</annotation></semantics></math> and draft distribution <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overset{\leftrightarrow}{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">↔</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overset{\leftrightarrow}{p}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that the joint probability over the output token and that an acceptance occurs is</span></p>
<table id="A3.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\bm{x},A)=\text{min}(\overset{\leftrightarrow}{p}(\bm{x}),\overset{\rightarrow}{p}(\bm{x}))," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">min</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">↔</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\bm{x},A)=\text{min}(\overset{\leftrightarrow}{p}(\bm{x}),\overset{\rightarrow}{p}(\bm{x})),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">while the joint probability over the output token and that a rejection occurs is</span></p>
<table id="A3.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\bm{x},R)=\text{max}(0,\overset{\rightarrow}{p}(\bm{x})-\overset{\leftrightarrow}{p}(\bm{x}))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">max</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">↔</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\bm{x},R)=\text{max}(0,\overset{\rightarrow}{p}(\bm{x})-\overset{\leftrightarrow}{p}(\bm{x}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">A single speculative sampling step consists of first sampling a draft token <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\bm{x}}\sim\overset{\leftrightarrow}{p}(\hat{\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">↔</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\bm{x}}\sim\overset{\leftrightarrow}{p}(\hat{\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math>, then accepting that token with probability <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{min}(1,\frac{\overset{\rightarrow}{p}(\hat{\bm{x}})}{\overset{\leftrightarrow}{p}(\hat{\bm{x}})})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>min</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo mathsize="0.710em" stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo mathsize="0.710em" stretchy="false">↔</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{min}(1,\frac{\overset{\rightarrow}{p}(\hat{\bm{x}})}{\overset{\leftrightarrow}{p}(\hat{\bm{x}})})</annotation></semantics></math>. If the token is rejected, then a new token is sampled from the resample distribution <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\bm{x}}\sim p_{\text{res}}(\tilde{\bm{x}})\propto\text{max}(0,\overset{\rightarrow}{p}(\tilde{\bm{x}})-\overset{\leftrightarrow}{p}(\tilde{\bm{x}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>res</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mtext>max</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">↔</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{x}}\sim p_{\text{res}}(\tilde{\bm{x}})\propto\text{max}(0,\overset{\rightarrow}{p}(\tilde{\bm{x}})-\overset{\leftrightarrow}{p}(\tilde{\bm{x}}))</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We introduce labels for all random variables involved in this procedure. We have the draft token <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>, a uniform random variable for making the accept/reject decision, <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, the resampled token <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\bm{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the accept/reject decision variable <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\in\{A,R\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\in\{A,R\}</annotation></semantics></math> and finally the output token <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">We can write a joint distribution over all variables involved as</span></p>
<table id="A3.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\hat{\bm{x}},U,\tilde{\bm{x}},Y,\bm{x})=p(\hat{\bm{x}})p(U)p(\tilde{\bm{x}})p(Y|U,\hat{\bm{x}})p(\bm{x}|\hat{\bm{x}},\tilde{\bm{x}},Y)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\hat{\bm{x}},U,\tilde{\bm{x}},Y,\bm{x})=p(\hat{\bm{x}})p(U)p(\tilde{\bm{x}})p(Y|U,\hat{\bm{x}})p(\bm{x}|\hat{\bm{x}},\tilde{\bm{x}},Y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">with <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\hat{\bm{x}})=\overset{\leftrightarrow}{p}(\hat{\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">↔</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\hat{\bm{x}})=\overset{\leftrightarrow}{p}(\hat{\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(U)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(U)</annotation></semantics></math> the uniform distribution on <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\tilde{\bm{x}})=p_{\text{res}}(\tilde{\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>res</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\tilde{\bm{x}})=p_{\text{res}}(\tilde{\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> and</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p(Y|U,\hat{\bm{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p(Y|U,\hat{\bm{x}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E29.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\updelta\{Y=A\}\updelta\left\{U&lt;\text{min}\left(1,\frac{\overset{\rightarrow}{p}(\hat{\bm{x}})}{\overset{\leftrightarrow}{p}(\hat{\bm{x}})}\right)\right\}+\updelta\{Y=R\}\updelta\left\{U&gt;\text{min}\left(1,\frac{\overset{\rightarrow}{p}(\hat{\bm{x}})}{\overset{\leftrightarrow}{p}(\hat{\bm{x}})}\right)\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">δ</mi><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mtext>min</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">↔</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">δ</mi><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mtext>min</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">↔</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\updelta\{Y=A\}\updelta\left\{U&lt;\text{min}\left(1,\frac{\overset{\rightarrow}{p}(\hat{\bm{x}})}{\overset{\leftrightarrow}{p}(\hat{\bm{x}})}\right)\right\}+\updelta\{Y=R\}\updelta\left\{U&gt;\text{min}\left(1,\frac{\overset{\rightarrow}{p}(\hat{\bm{x}})}{\overset{\leftrightarrow}{p}(\hat{\bm{x}})}\right)\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p(\bm{x}|\hat{\bm{x}},\tilde{\bm{x}},Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p(\bm{x}|\hat{\bm{x}},\tilde{\bm{x}},Y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E30.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\updelta\{\bm{x}=\hat{\bm{x}}\}\updelta\{Y=A\}+\updelta\{\bm{x}=\tilde{\bm{x}}\}\updelta\{Y=R\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\updelta\{\bm{x}=\hat{\bm{x}}\}\updelta\{Y=A\}+\updelta\{\bm{x}=\tilde{\bm{x}}\}\updelta\{Y=R\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\updelta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\updelta</annotation></semantics></math> is the Kronecker delta.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">We first find <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\bm{x},A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\bm{x},A)</annotation></semantics></math> by summing/integrating out all other variables and setting <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=A</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p(\bm{x},A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p(\bm{x},A)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{\hat{\bm{x}}}\int_{U=0}^{U=1}\sum_{\tilde{\bm{x}}}p(\hat{\bm{x}},U,\tilde{\bm{x}},Y=A,\bm{x})\mathrm{d}U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{\hat{\bm{x}}}\int_{U=0}^{U=1}\sum_{\tilde{\bm{x}}}p(\hat{\bm{x}},U,\tilde{\bm{x}},Y=A,\bm{x})\mathrm{d}U</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E32.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{\hat{\bm{x}}}\int_{U=0}^{U=1}\sum_{\tilde{\bm{x}}}\overset{\leftrightarrow}{p}(\hat{\bm{x}})p_{\text{res}}(\tilde{\bm{x}})\updelta\left\{U&lt;\text{min}\left(1,\frac{\overset{\rightarrow}{p}(\hat{\bm{x}})}{\overset{\leftrightarrow}{p}(\hat{\bm{x}})}\right)\right\}\updelta\{\bm{x}=\hat{\bm{x}}\}\mathrm{d}U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></munder></mstyle><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">↔</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>res</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">δ</mi><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mtext>min</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">↔</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{\hat{\bm{x}}}\int_{U=0}^{U=1}\sum_{\tilde{\bm{x}}}\overset{\leftrightarrow}{p}(\hat{\bm{x}})p_{\text{res}}(\tilde{\bm{x}})\updelta\left\{U&lt;\text{min}\left(1,\frac{\overset{\rightarrow}{p}(\hat{\bm{x}})}{\overset{\leftrightarrow}{p}(\hat{\bm{x}})}\right)\right\}\updelta\{\bm{x}=\hat{\bm{x}}\}\mathrm{d}U</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E33.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{\hat{\bm{x}}}\overset{\leftrightarrow}{p}(\hat{\bm{x}})\updelta\{\bm{x}=\hat{\bm{x}}\}\int_{U=0}^{U=1}\updelta\left\{U&lt;\text{min}\left(1,\frac{\overset{\rightarrow}{p}(\hat{\bm{x}})}{\overset{\leftrightarrow}{p}(\hat{\bm{x}})}\right)\right\}\mathrm{d}U\underbrace{\sum_{\tilde{\bm{x}}}p_{\text{res}}(\tilde{\bm{x}})}_{=1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></munder></mstyle><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">↔</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mi mathvariant="normal">δ</mi><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>U</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mtext>min</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">→</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">↔</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>U</mi><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>res</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{\hat{\bm{x}}}\overset{\leftrightarrow}{p}(\hat{\bm{x}})\updelta\{\bm{x}=\hat{\bm{x}}\}\int_{U=0}^{U=1}\updelta\left\{U&lt;\text{min}\left(1,\frac{\overset{\rightarrow}{p}(\hat{\bm{x}})}{\overset{\leftrightarrow}{p}(\hat{\bm{x}})}\right)\right\}\mathrm{d}U\underbrace{\sum_{\tilde{\bm{x}}}p_{\text{res}}(\tilde{\bm{x}})}_{=1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
